=begin
  eohunter: a hunting script on an engine built piece by piece from
  bigshot's rules. The engine lives in scripts/eohunter/*.rb (namespace
  EO::Engine); this file wires a bigshot profile to it and runs the loop.

    ;eohunter <profile>                    hunt with data/<game>/<char>/bigshot_profiles/<profile>.yaml
    ;eohunter <profile> dry                load the profile, report the policies, do not run
    ;eohunter <profile> bandits            hunt bandits (also on when the bounty says so)
    ;eohunter <profile> track <creature>   Rangers: TRACK toward the creature before each step
    ;eohunter <profile> head <count>       lead a group: wait for <count> followers, then hunt
    ;eohunter <profile> head <name> ...    lead a group of these characters
    ;eohunter <profile> head <count> lan   ...and serve the rally hub to the
                                           network, for followers on other machines
    ;eohunter <profile> tail [uri]         follow a leader (the rally whisper names the uri)
    ;eohunter bounty [<creature>] [head|tail]   ebounty's hunt child, as "bigshot bounty": the profile
                                           ebounty put in UserVars.op, its bounty_eval, exit at rest

  Behaviors by priority: Survival 0, Cleanse 5 (ecleanse folded in; its
  settings from ecleanse.yaml), Flee 10, Muster 15 (the leader's holds),
  Rest 20 (a follower's Orders), Loot 30, Loadout 35, Maintain 40, Engage 50 (a
  follower's Assist), Wander 60 (a follower's Follow). One action per
  tick; the most urgent behavior that wants control gets the tick.

        author: elanthia-online
  contributors: Nisugi
          game: Gemstone
          tags: hunting, combat, eo
      required: Lich >= 5.20.1
       version: 0.5.1

  Version Control:
  Major_change.feature_addition.bugfix
  v0.5.1 (2026-09-10)
    - group liveness pulses between ticks (a blocking action no longer reads
      as a lost member or dead leader); a follower's hunting_scripts_stop no
      longer fogs; the group bounty rests on the verdict alone
    - the engine acts on nothing after a tick callback stops it, and announces
      the room before choosing a behavior (a follower's room resets too)
    - Cleanse never runs a job after a spent trip; flee_message matches as a
      pattern; boons_ignore / boons_flee read ASSESS (sent by Engage, never
      from a predicate); 411 casts on the weapon; wand_if_oom waves the wand
  v0.5.0 (2026-09-10)
    - core only: the send ladder is fput's (#1587), the watch rules are
      Combat::Messages, :ucs and :attack subscriptions (#1586), the fog is
      Lich's Fog (#1584); requires the eohunter test package until they merge
  v0.4.0 (2026-09-10)
    - bounty: the hunt child ebounty runs in place of bigshot bounty (profile
      and bounty_eval from UserVars.op, bandits from the bounty, exit at rest)
    - group: each member's bounty state, the leader's verdict (a lost member
      before a complete bounty), the acknowledged shutdown
  v0.3.0 (2026-09-10)
    - group hunting: head and tail, bigshot's leader waits and follower
      events as orders over DRb, the looter choice, group deader, the
      group half of Troubadour's Rally
  v0.2.2 (2026-09-10)
    - bandit hunting (the quick routine, no flee) and Ranger tracking
    - Troubadour's Rally: 1040 on ourselves when webbed, sleeping, stunned or frozen
  v0.2.1 (2026-09-10)
    - the final loot is a Rest phase (Rest outranked Loot, so it never ran)
    - a preempted behavior's trip is suspended (go2 killed) and resumes after
    - Cleanse's disarm, itchy curse and vat trips are supervised trips
    - libeo only when Lich has no Fog module; custom fog is Rest's own phase
  v0.2.0 (2026-09-10)
    - the M0 spike: a bigshot profile into the seven behaviors, the engine loop
    - Cleanse: ecleanse 2.3.6 folded in at priority 5, reading ecleanse.yaml
  v0.1.0 (2026-09-10)
    - initial: loads the engine, installs the watch, reports the parts
=end

# The engine consumes lich-5 #1578-#1587 (Stance, Stash, Mana.pulse, Bank,
# the PSM readers, Fog, the spell refresh, Combat::Messages, bounded
# fput): a Lich without them is the eohunter test package's job, not a
# stand-in's.
%w[Lich::Gemstone::Fog Lich::Gemstone::Combat::Messages Lich::Gemstone::Stance Lich::Gemstone::Mana].each do |const|
  next if Object.const_defined?(const)

  Lich::Messaging.msg('error', "eohunter: this Lich lacks #{const}; install the eohunter test package (github.com/Nisugi/lich-5/releases)")
  exit
end

# Before the load below, which does remove_const on EO::Engine. Ruby
# resolves constants at call time, so a second instance gives the first
# one's before_dying a *different* Watch and Events: killing the older
# instance then uninstalls the live one's tracker handlers, its
# DownstreamHook and its event bus, and the running hunt goes silently
# deaf to every combat fact, disarm and flee line with nothing reported.
me = Script.current
if (running = Script.list.select { |s| s.name == me.name && !s.equal?(me) }).any?
  Lich::Messaging.msg('error', "eohunter: already running (#{running.size} other). ;kill eohunter first, or use its ;pause and ;unpause.")
  exit
end

require 'drb'
load File.join(SCRIPT_DIR, 'eohunter', 'engine.rb')

# The script's own glue: wires a bigshot profile to the engine, reports
# it, leads or follows a group, and runs the loop (supervised or not).
module EOHunter
  # Short name for the engine namespace.
  E = EO::Engine
    # LAB scans these exact declarations without evaluating the script.
    # rubocop:disable Layout/IndentationWidth, Layout/IndentationConsistency
    # The supervised controller protocol version LAB matches against.
    SUPERVISED_CONTROLLER_PROTOCOL = 1
    # The refuge start protocol version LAB matches against.
    REFUGE_START_PROTOCOL = 1
  # rubocop:enable Layout/IndentationWidth, Layout/IndentationConsistency
  # Seconds the leader waits for the followers to register (bigshot head 9897).
  RALLY_TIMEOUT = 60 # bigshot head 9897
  # Seconds between rally whispers (bigshot head 9899).
  RALLY_EVERY = 3 # bigshot head 9899
  # The leader's rally whisper, capturing the DRb uri.
  RALLY_LINE = %r{eohunter rallying at (druby://[^\s"<]+?)\.?["<]}i

  # A front-end line with the "eohunter: " prefix.
  # @param kind [String] Lich::Messaging kind (info, warn, error, debug)
  # @param text [String]
  # @return [void]
  def self.msg(kind, text) = Lich::Messaging.msg(kind, "eohunter: #{text}")

  # Where this character's bigshot profile lives.
  # @param name [String] the profile name
  # @return [String] data/<game>/<char>/bigshot_profiles/<name>.yaml
  def self.profile_path(name)
    File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'bigshot_profiles', "#{name}.yaml")
  end

  # Every event worth a line in the front end, and the few that change
  # what the engine does next.
  #
  # @param engine [E::Engine] stopped on hunt_over, a death or a deader
  # @param behaviors [Hash{Symbol => Object}] build's hash; :rest takes the
  #   forced rest reasons
  # @return [void]
  def self.wire(engine, behaviors)
    rest = behaviors[:rest]
    rest_policy = behaviors[:rest_policy]
    loadout = behaviors[:loadout]
    member = behaviors[:member]
    follower_return_prepped = false
    loadout_stranded = false
    # Every wait inside an action checks this, and nothing ever set it, so
    # stop! could not shorten an fput or a roundtime wait already in
    # flight and every interrupted? guard in the engine was inert.
    E::Actions::Base.interrupt = -> { engine.stopping? }
    # The bus isolates a handler's exception and hands it to a reporter
    # that defaulted to nil, so an error in any of the handlers below -
    # the CharSettings write, a nil in a payload, rest! raising -
    # disappeared with no front-end line and nothing in the log.
    E::Events.error_reporter = ->(type, error) { msg('error', "handler for #{type} raised #{error.class}: #{error.message}") }
    E::Events.on(:engine_started) { |e| msg('info', "hunting: #{e.data[:behaviors].join(', ')}") }
    E::Events.on(:engine_stopped) { |e| msg('warn', "stopped: #{e.data[:reason]}") }
    E::Events.on(:engine_error) { |e| msg('error', "#{e.data[:error]}: #{e.data[:message]}\n  #{Array(e.data[:backtrace]).join("\n  ")}") }
    E::Events.on(:watchdog_tripped) do |e|
      because = e.data[:reason] ? ": #{e.data[:reason]}" : ''
      answer = e.data[:line].to_s.strip
      msg('error', "watchdog: #{e.data[:kind]} in #{e.data[:behavior]} (#{e.data[:count]})#{because}")
      msg('error', "  the game said: #{answer}") unless answer.empty?
      declined = Array(e.data[:evaluations]).reject { |_n, wanted| wanted }.map(&:first)
      msg('error', "  declined above it: #{declined.join(', ')}") unless declined.empty?
    end
    E::Events.on(:engaged) { |e| msg('info', "engaging #{e.data[:name]} (routine #{e.data[:routine]})") }
    E::Events.on(:fleeing) { |e| msg('warn', "fleeing: #{e.data[:reason]}") }
    E::Events.on(:cleansing) { |e| msg('warn', "cleanse: #{e.data[:reason]}") }
    E::Events.on(:cleansed) { |e| msg('debug', "cleanse #{e.data[:reason]}: #{e.data[:result]}") }
    E::Events.on(:disarmed) { |e| msg('error', "DISARMED: #{e.data[:noun]} in room #{e.data[:room]}") }
    E::Events.on(:cleanse_stuck) { |e| msg('error', e.data[:reason]); rest.rest!(e.data[:reason]) if rest.respond_to?(:rest!) }
    E::Events.on(:loadout_stuck) do |e|
      detail = e.data[:message].to_s.empty? ? e.data[:reason] : e.data[:message]
      reason = "loadout #{e.data[:wanted]}: #{detail}"
      msg('error', reason)
      refuge = member ? member.rooms[:resting] : rest_policy&.resting_room
      if member || (refuge && e.data[:room].to_s != refuge.to_s)
        rest.rest!(reason)
      else
        engine.stop!(:loadout_stuck)
      end
    end
    if loadout
      rest.prepare_hands = loadout.method(:prepare) unless member
      combat = behaviors[:engage]
      if combat.respond_to?(:equipment_interrupt=)
        urgent = behaviors.values_at(:survival, :cleanse, :flee).compact
        # Recovery waits inside an action; poll only the urgent predicates
        # and existing lifecycle state so the next arbiter tick can take over.
        combat.equipment_interrupt = lambda do |world|
          engine.stopping? || engine.paused? || rest.resting? || urgent.any? { |behavior| behavior.wants_control?(world) }
        end
      end
      E::Events.on(:rest_stranded) { loadout_stranded = true if loadout.stuck? }
      E::Events.on(:order) do |event|
        follower_return_prepped = true if loadout.stuck? && event.data[:type] == :resting_prep
      end if member
      engine.on_tick do |world|
        next unless loadout.stuck?
        next if E::Travel.active&.underway?

        refuge = member ? member.rooms[:resting] : rest_policy&.resting_room
        ready = member ? follower_return_prepped && rest.rest_prep_done && rest.phase == :idle : rest.phase == :resting
        if ready && loadout_stranded
          msg('error', 'loadout recovery stranded: refuge was not reached; manual intervention required')
          engine.stop!(:loadout_return_failed)
        elsif ready && refuge && world.room.id.to_s == refuge.to_s
          engine.stop!(:loadout_stuck)
        end
      end
    end
    E::Events.on(:rest_started) do |e|
      msg('info', "resting: #{e.data[:reason]}")
      Array(e.data[:followers]).each { |n, r| msg('info', " #{n} resting: #{r}") }
    end
    E::Events.on(:resting) do |e|
      msg('debug', "still resting: #{e.data[:reason]}") if e.data[:reason]
      Array(e.data[:followers]).each { |n, r| msg('debug', " #{n} isn't hunting because: #{r}") }
    end
    E::Events.on(:rest_finished) { msg('info', 'hunting again') }
    E::Events.on(:rest_stuck) { |e| msg('error', "could not reach #{e.data[:room]}") }
    E::Events.on(:rest_retry) { |e| msg('warn', "trying #{e.data[:room]} again (#{e.data[:attempt]} of #{e.data[:of]})") }
    E::Events.on(:rest_stranded) { |e| msg('error', "stranded: could not reach #{e.data[:room]} from #{e.data[:here]}; resting here, not reported as rested") }
    E::Events.on(:out_of_bounds) { |e| msg('warn', "out of bounds in #{e.data[:room]}, heading for #{e.data[:hunting_room]}") }
    E::Events.on(:travel_failed) { |e| msg('error', "go2 #{e.data[:place]} failed #{e.data[:attempts]} times") }
    E::Events.on(:loot_script_started) { |e| msg('debug', "loot: #{e.data[:script]}") }
    E::Events.on(:routine_unsupported) { |e| msg('warn', "routine word not built yet, skipped: #{e.data[:command]}") }
    E::Events.on(:untargetable_learned) do |e|
      CharSettings['untargetable'] ||= []
      CharSettings['untargetable'] |= [e.data[:name]]
      msg('warn', "learned untargetable: #{e.data[:name]}")
    end
    # bigshot's forced rest reasons ($bigshot_should_rest)
    if rest.respond_to?(:rest!)
      E::Events.on(:out_of_mana) { rest.rest!('out of mana') }
      E::Events.on(:loot_stuck) { |e| rest.rest!(e.data[:reason]) }
      E::Events.on(:maintain_stuck) { |e| rest.rest!(e.data[:reason]) }
      E::Events.on(:too_many_items) { rest.rest!('Too many items') }
      # Only when a rest is not already under way: Rest emits :rest_stuck
      # mid-rest, and a forced reason survives finish (only begin_rest
      # clears it), so re-arming here meant a stranded rest was followed
      # by an immediate second one and the hunter never fought again.
      E::Events.on(:rest_stuck) { |e| rest.rest!("Could not reach #{e.data[:room]}") unless rest.resting? }
      E::Events.on(:too_injured_for_wands) { rest.rest!('Too injured to wave wands!') }
      E::Events.on(:no_fresh_wands) { rest.rest!('No fresh wands!') }
      E::Events.on(:ammo_no_effect) { rest.rest!('Ammo had no effect (need blessed or magical)') }
    end
    E::Events.on(:preempted) { |e| msg('debug', "#{e.data[:to] || 'idle'} took control from #{e.data[:from]}") }
    E::Events.on(:tracked) { |e| msg('info', "tracked #{e.data[:creature]}: #{e.data[:outcome]} in #{e.data[:room]}") }
    # group
    E::Events.on(:waiting_for_followers) { |e| msg('warn', "waiting for followers: #{e.data[:reason]}") }
    E::Events.on(:followers_ready) { |e| msg('debug', "followers ready: #{e.data[:reason]}") }
    E::Events.on(:follower_lost) { |e| msg('error', "follower #{e.data[:name]} has stopped answering; not waiting for them") }
    E::Events.on(:loot_assigned) { |e| msg('info', "#{e.data[:looter]} loots this room") }
    E::Events.on(:order) { |e| msg('debug', "order: #{e.data[:type]}#{e.data[:payload] ? " #{e.data[:payload]}" : ''}") }
    E::Events.on(:hunt_over) { |e| msg('warn', "the leader ended the hunt: #{e.data[:reason]}"); engine.stop!(:hunt_over) }
    E::Events.on(:hunt_ended) { |e| msg('warn', "hunt ended: #{e.data[:reason]}#{e.data[:unacked].any? ? "; never answered: #{e.data[:unacked].join(', ')}" : ''}") }
    E::Events.on(:rested) { |e| msg('info', "rested: #{e.data[:reason]}") }
    E::Events.on(:died) { |e| msg('error', "dead (#{e.data[:on_death]})"); engine.stop!(:dead) if e.data[:on_death] == :stop }
    E::Events.on(:deader) { |e| msg('error', "dead player here: #{e.data[:players].join(', ')} - ;pause eohunter is bigshot's answer; stopping"); engine.stop!(:deader) }
  end

  # The profile into the leader's (or solo) behaviors: Survival, Cleanse,
  # Flee, Rest, Loot, Maintain, Engage, Wander, the area, and Muster when
  # leading.
  #
  # @param profile [E::Profile] the loaded bigshot profile
  # @param world [E::World]
  # @param tracking [E::Tracking::Policy] bandit mode and the Ranger's quarry
  # @param leader [E::Group::Leader, nil] when leading a group
  # @param scripts [E::Controller::ChildScripts, nil] the controlled child
  #   seam; nil uses Lich's Script and a Travel trip
  # @param trial [E::Controller::TrialSequence, nil] Engage's routine selector
  # @return [Hash{Symbol => Object}] the behaviors by name, plus :area
  def self.build(profile, world, tracking: E::Tracking::Policy.new, leader: nil, scripts: nil, trial: nil)
    untargetable = Array(CharSettings['untargetable'])
    targets_policy = profile.targets_policy(untargetable: untargetable)
    # boons_ignore / boons_flee read a creature's abilities from one ASSESS (check_boons 8082), sent by Engage
    targets_policy.boon_abilities = E::Targets::BoonCache.new(world)
    # bandit mode (bigshot sort_npcs 8622, priority 8675, should_flee? 8540):
    # only the bandit nouns, on the quick routine, never switching, never fleeing
    targets_policy.wanted = E::Tracking.bandit_targets if tracking.bandits?
    wander_policy = profile.wander_policy
    rest_policy = profile.rest_policy(wounded_binding: binding)
    walker = E::Wander::Walker.new(boundaries: wander_policy.boundary_ids)
    area = E::Wander::Area.new(start: wander_policy.hunting_room, boundaries: wander_policy.boundary_ids).build(world)
    engage_state = E::Engage::State.new
    maintain_state = E::Maintain::State.new
    counters = E::Rest::Counters.new
    travel = scripts && ->(room) { E::Travel::Trip.new(room, scripts: scripts) }
    loot = E::Behaviors::Loot.new(policy: profile.loot_policy, targets_policy: targets_policy, rest_policy: rest_policy,
                                  counters: counters, group: leader, scripts: scripts)
    # Rest drives Loot for the final loot before leaving (should_rest? 9041)
    rest = E::Behaviors::Rest.new(policy: rest_policy, counters: counters, loot: loot, group: leader,
                                  scripts: scripts, travel: travel)
    cleanse_policy = E::Cleanse::Policy.load(File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'ecleanse.yaml'), char_settings: CharSettings.to_hash)
    # bigshot's Troubadour's Rally toggle: 1040 on ourselves and the group
    cleanse_policy.troubadours_rally = profile['troubadours_rally']
    cleanse = E::Behaviors::Cleanse.new(policy: cleanse_policy, travel: travel)
    survival = E::Behaviors::Survival.new(policy: profile.survival_policy, resting: -> { rest.resting? })
    flee_policy = profile.flee_policy
    flee_policy.bandits = tracking.bandits?
    flee = E::Behaviors::Flee.new(policy: flee_policy, targets_policy: targets_policy, walker: walker,
                                  group_nouns: -> { world.group_nouns },
                                  wander_stance: wander_policy.wander_stance)
    maintain = E::Behaviors::Maintain.new(policy: profile.maintain_policy, state: maintain_state)
    engage_policy = profile.engage_policy
    engage_policy.priority = false if tracking.bandits?
    engage = E::Behaviors::Engage.new(policy: engage_policy, targets_policy: targets_policy, wander_policy: wander_policy,
                                      mstrike_policy: profile.mstrike_policy, state: engage_state,
                                      maintain_state: maintain_state, group: leader,
                                      fried: -> { E::Rest::Predicates.fried?(world.me, rest_policy) },
                                      routine_selector: trial && trial.method(:select))
    loadout = E::Behaviors::Loadout.new(policy: profile.loadout_policy, selection: profile.loadout_selection,
                                        owner: engage, resting: -> { rest.resting? })
    engage.on_fight { flee.engaged! }
    wander = E::Behaviors::Wander.new(policy: wander_policy, targets_policy: targets_policy, walker: walker,
                                      area: area, tracking: tracking, travel: travel, state: engage_state)
    behaviors = { survival: survival, cleanse: cleanse, flee: flee, rest: rest, loot: loot, loadout: loadout,
                  maintain: maintain, engage: engage, wander: wander, area: area, rest_policy: rest_policy }
    if leader
      behaviors[:muster] = E::Behaviors::Muster.new(leader: leader, resting: -> { rest.resting? },
                                                    fight: ->(w) { E::Wander::Predicates.fight_here?(w, targets_policy, wander_policy) })
    end
    behaviors
  end

  # One observation of the character for the controller's guard: session
  # identity, room and its epoch, ownership, connection, life, posture,
  # the two hand ids, stability (same room before and after the reads,
  # never room 4) and whether the room is safe to be left in.
  #
  # @param owner [Script] the eohunter script instance
  # @param session [String] the launch token
  # @return [Hash{Symbol => Object}] session, room_id, room_epoch, owner,
  #   connected, alive, standing, hands, stable, destination_safe
  def self.controller_snapshot(owner, session)
    epoch = XMLData.room_count
    room = Room.current&.id
    hands = [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].map { |item| item&.id&.to_s }
    alive = !Lich::Gemstone::Status.dead? && Char.health.to_i.positive? && Char.spirit.to_i.positive?
    # The hostile flag lives on Lich's CreatureInstance (crtrStatus), not
    # on the GameObj room object, so ask the creature registry for it.
    hostile = Array(GameObj.targets).any? || Array(GameObj.hidden_targets).any? || Lich::Gemstone::Overwatch.hiders? || Array(GameObj.npcs).any? do |npc|
      next false if npc.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/

      instance = Lich::Gemstone::Creature[npc.id.to_s]
      instance.respond_to?(:crtr_flag?) && instance.crtr_flag?(:hostile) == true
    end
    stable = room && room != 4 && epoch == XMLData.room_count && room == Room.current&.id
    {
      session: "#{session}:#{XMLData.game}:#{Char.name}", room_id: room, room_epoch: epoch,
      owner: Script.list.include?(owner), connected: !Game.closed?, alive: alive,
      standing: XMLData.indicator['IconSTANDING'] == 'y', hands: hands,
      stable: stable == true, destination_safe: stable == true && alive && !hostile
    }
  end

  # The supervised run: build the Runtime, publish it on the owner script
  # as controller_runtime and controller_refuge_travel_child? for LAB and
  # Lich to find, run it, then publish the result as controller_result and
  # remove the two methods again.
  #
  # @param engine [E::Engine]
  # @param behaviors [Hash{Symbol => Object}] build's hash; :rest is required
  # @param world [E::World]
  # @param owner [Script] the eohunter script instance
  # @param launch [E::Controller::Launch]
  # @param children [E::Controller::ChildScripts]
  # @param guard [E::Controller::Guard]
  # @param objective [E::Controller::TrialSequence]
  # @param snapshot [Proc] -> Hash; the controller_snapshot lambda
  # @return [Hash] the runtime's final status
  # @raise [E::Controller::Invalid] the owner lacks Lich's execution guards
  #   or child lifecycle, a guard is already active, or a runtime or result
  #   is already published on it
  def self.run_controlled(engine:, behaviors:, world:, owner:, launch:, children:, guard:, objective:, snapshot:)
    unless %i[with_execution_guard execution_guard_active? execution_sleep stopping? child_scripts].all? { |name| owner.respond_to?(name) } &&
           Script.respond_to?(:start_child) && !owner.execution_guard_active?
      raise E::Controller::Invalid, 'controlled eohunter requires native Lich execution guards and exact child lifecycle'
    end
    raise E::Controller::Invalid, 'controlled runtime is already published on this owner' if owner.respond_to?(:controller_runtime, true)
    raise E::Controller::Invalid, 'controlled result is already published on this owner' if owner.respond_to?(:controller_result, true)

    runtime = E::Controller::Runtime.new(engine: engine, rest: behaviors.fetch(:rest), world: world,
                                         owner: owner, guard: guard, children: children,
                                         launch: launch, objective: objective, snapshot: snapshot)
    predicate = ->(candidate) { children.active_travel_child?(candidate) }
    owner.define_singleton_method(:controller_runtime) { runtime }
    runtime_method = owner.method(:controller_runtime)
    owner.define_singleton_method(:controller_refuge_travel_child?) { |candidate| predicate.call(candidate) }
    travel_method = owner.method(:controller_refuge_travel_child?)
    runtime.run
  ensure
    result = runtime&.close
    owner.define_singleton_method(:controller_result) { result } if owner && result && !owner.respond_to?(:controller_result, true)
    if runtime_method && owner.respond_to?(:controller_runtime) && owner.method(:controller_runtime) == runtime_method
      owner.singleton_class.remove_method(:controller_runtime)
    end
    if travel_method && owner.respond_to?(:controller_refuge_travel_child?) && owner.method(:controller_refuge_travel_child?) == travel_method
      owner.singleton_class.remove_method(:controller_refuge_travel_child?)
    end
  end

  # A follower (bigshot tail 9973): the same Survival, Cleanse, Flee and
  # Maintain; Orders for Rest, Assist for Engage, Follow for Wander, Loot
  # only when assigned.
  #
  # @bigshot tail 9973
  # @param profile [E::Profile]
  # @param world [E::World]
  # @param member [E::Group::Member] our registration with the leader's hub
  # @return [Hash{Symbol => Object}] the behaviors by name, plus :rest_policy,
  #   :counters and :sneaky for the follower's reports
  def self.build_follower(profile, world, member)
    untargetable = Array(CharSettings['untargetable'])
    targets_policy = profile.targets_policy(untargetable: untargetable)
    targets_policy.boon_abilities = E::Targets::BoonCache.new(world)
    wander_policy = profile.wander_policy
    walker = E::Wander::Walker.new(boundaries: wander_policy.boundary_ids)
    maintain_state = E::Maintain::State.new
    counters = E::Rest::Counters.new
    rest_policy = profile.rest_policy(wounded_binding: binding)
    loot = E::Behaviors::Loot.new(policy: profile.loot_policy, targets_policy: targets_policy, rest_policy: rest_policy, counters: counters, follower: true)
    assist = E::Behaviors::Assist.new(member: member, policy: profile.engage_policy, targets_policy: targets_policy, wander_policy: wander_policy,
                                      mstrike_policy: profile.mstrike_policy, maintain_state: maintain_state)
    follow = E::Behaviors::Follow.new(member: member)
    orders = E::Behaviors::Orders.new(member: member, policy: rest_policy, counters: counters, assist: assist, follow: follow, loot: loot,
                                      sneaky: wander_policy.sneaky)
    loadout = E::Behaviors::Loadout.new(policy: profile.loadout_policy, selection: profile.loadout_selection,
                                        owner: assist, resting: -> { orders.resting? })
    cleanse_policy = E::Cleanse::Policy.load(File.join(DATA_DIR, XMLData.game, Char.name, 'ecleanse.yaml'), char_settings: CharSettings.to_hash)
    cleanse_policy.troubadours_rally = profile['troubadours_rally']
    cleanse = E::Behaviors::Cleanse.new(policy: cleanse_policy)
    survival = E::Behaviors::Survival.new(policy: profile.survival_policy, resting: -> { orders.resting? }, follower: true)
    flee = E::Behaviors::Flee.new(policy: profile.flee_policy, targets_policy: targets_policy, walker: walker,
                                  group_nouns: -> { world.group_nouns },
                                  wander_stance: wander_policy.wander_stance)
    maintain = E::Behaviors::Maintain.new(policy: profile.maintain_policy, state: maintain_state)
    assist.on_fight { flee.engaged! }
    { survival: survival, cleanse: cleanse, flee: flee, rest: orders, loot: loot, loadout: loadout,
      maintain: maintain, engage: assist, wander: follow,
      rest_policy: rest_policy, counters: counters, sneaky: wander_policy.sneaky, member: member }
  end

  # The profile summary in the front end: rooms and area size, targets,
  # the routines, signs, loot and rest, and where an unbounded area
  # crosses into another location.
  #
  # @param profile [E::Profile]
  # @param behaviors [Hash{Symbol => Object}] build's hash; :area is read
  # @return [void]
  def self.report(profile, behaviors)
    area = behaviors[:area]
    msg('info', "profile #{profile.name}: hunting room #{profile['hunting_room_id']}, boundaries #{profile['hunting_boundaries'].join(', ')}, area #{area.rooms&.size || 0} rooms#{area.too_big? ? ' (TOO BIG: a boundary is missing)' : ''}")
    msg('info', "targets: #{profile['targets'].map { |k, v| "#{k}(#{v})" }.join(', ')}")
    ('a'..'j').each do |l|
      list = profile.engage_policy.routines[l]
      msg('info', "routine #{l}: #{list.join(' | ')}") if list && !list.empty?
    end
    msg('info', "signs: #{profile['signs'].join(', ')}; loot: #{profile['loot_script'] || 'loot'}#{profile['delay_loot'] ? ' (delayed)' : ''}; rest at #{profile['resting_room_id']}")
    loadout = profile.loadout_policy
    msg('info', "hunting loadout: #{loadout.description}") if loadout.managed?
    if profile['hunting_loadout_rules'].any?
      msg('info', "hunting loadout rules: #{profile['hunting_loadout_rules'].size} (in profile order)")
    end
    area.location_changes.each { |c| msg('warn', "area crosses into #{c[:location]} at room #{c[:id]}") } if area.too_big?
  end

  # bigshot head (9876-9972): group open, serve the hub, whisper the uri
  # to the group until everyone expected has registered. Exits the script
  # with no group to lead or when the rally times out.
  #
  # @bigshot head 9876-9972
  # @param profile [E::Profile] the rally, hunting, waypoint and resting rooms
  # @param world [E::World]
  # @param args [Array<String>] a follower count, follower names, or nothing
  #   (the current group)
  # @return [E::Group::Leader] the activated group
  def self.lead(profile, world, args)
    # The Hub is served on the loopback address unless the profile's
    # group spans machines: 'head 2 lan' opts back in to all interfaces.
    lan = args.reject! { |a| a.to_s.casecmp('lan').zero? } ? true : false
    E::Actions::GroupOpen.new(world).call
    E::Actions::Command.new(world, command: 'unhide').call if world.me.hidden?
    expected = if args.first.to_s =~ /\A\d+\z/ then args.first.to_i
               elsif args.any? then args.map { |n| n.to_s.capitalize }
               else
                 Lich::Gemstone::Group.check
                 world.group_nouns.size
               end
    if expected == 0 || (expected.is_a?(Array) && expected.empty?)
      msg('error', 'no group to lead: ;eohunter <profile> head <count> or head <name> <name>')
      exit
    end
    hub = E::Group::Hub.new
    # A nil URI binds every interface, so anyone who can reach the port
    # can drive a follower through the Hub: it answers orders with no
    # authentication, and Order carries a :command type that runs an
    # arbitrary game command (group.rb 1302). Nothing in the engine ever
    # sends that order - the leader has fourteen types and :command is
    # not among them - so the exposure is the whole reachable surface,
    # not one handler. Loopback by default; 'lan' opts back in.
    DRb.start_service(lan ? nil : 'druby://127.0.0.1:0', hub)
    uri = DRb.uri
    rooms = { rally: profile['rallypoint_room_ids'], hunting: profile['hunting_room_id'],
              waypoints: profile['return_waypoint_ids'], resting: profile['resting_room_id'] }
    hub.open_hunt(leader: Char.name, expected: expected, rooms: rooms)
    msg('info', "leading #{expected.is_a?(Integer) ? "#{expected} followers" : expected.join(', ')}; rallying at #{uri}")
    deadline = Time.now + RALLY_TIMEOUT
    until hub.ready?
      if Time.now > deadline
        msg('error', "rally timed out; missing: #{hub.missing.join(', ')}")
        exit
      end
      Lich::Util.issue_command("whisper ooc group eohunter rallying at #{uri}", /<pushStream id="speech"/, silent: true, quiet: false)
      sleep RALLY_EVERY
    end
    hub.activate!
    msg('info', "group: #{hub.members.join(', ')}")
    E::Group::Leader.new(hub, name: Char.name, policy: profile.group_policy)
  end

  # bigshot tail (9973-10045): the rally whisper names the uri unless
  # given; connect, register until the hunt is open, wait for it to start.
  # Exits the script when no whisper comes, the leader stops answering,
  # or registration fails.
  #
  # @bigshot tail 9973-10045
  # @param args [Array<String>] an optional druby:// uri
  # @return [E::Group::Member] our registration, once the hunt is active
  #   or the wait for it timed out
  def self.follow(args)
    uri = args.first.to_s =~ %r{\Adruby://} ? args.first : nil
    unless uri
      hook = proc do |line|
        uri = Regexp.last_match(1) if uri.nil? && line =~ RALLY_LINE
        line
      end
      DownstreamHook.add('eohunter::rally', hook)
      msg('info', 'waiting for the leader\'s rally whisper')
      deadline = Time.now + RALLY_TIMEOUT * 2
      sleep 0.5 while uri.nil? && Time.now < deadline
      DownstreamHook.remove('eohunter::rally')
      if uri.nil?
        msg('error', 'no rally whisper seen; ;eohunter <profile> tail <uri> names it')
        exit
      end
    end
    DRb.start_service
    hub = DRbObject.new_with_uri(uri)
    member = E::Group::Member.new(hub, name: Char.name)
    msg('info', "joining the group at #{uri}")
    120.times do
      break if member.register
      if member.lost?
        msg('error', 'the leader is not answering')
        exit
      end
      sleep 0.5
    end
    unless member.registered?
      msg('error', 'could not join the hunt')
      exit
    end
    msg('info', "joined #{member.leader_name}'s hunt #{member.hunt_id}; waiting for the start")
    deadline = Time.now + RALLY_TIMEOUT * 2
    sleep 0.5 until (hub.active? rescue false) || Time.now > deadline
    member
  end
end

name = script.vars[1].to_s
options = script.vars[2..].to_a.map(&:to_s)
controlled, options = EO::Engine::Controller::Launch.extract!(options)
trial, options = EO::Engine::Controller::TrialSequence.extract!(options)
dry = options.any? { |o| o =~ /^dry$/i }
if name.empty?
  EOHunter.msg('error', 'usage: ;eohunter <profile> [dry] [bandits] [track <creature>] [head <count> [lan]|tail [uri]]  or  ;eohunter bounty [<creature>] [head <count>|tail]')
  exit
end
mode_at = options.index { |o| o =~ /^(head|lead|tail|follow)$/i }
mode = mode_at && options[mode_at].downcase
mode_args = mode_at ? options[(mode_at + 1)..] : []
mode = 'head' if mode == 'lead'
mode = 'tail' if mode == 'follow'
options = options[0...mode_at] if mode_at
if trial && !controlled
  raise EO::Engine::Controller::Invalid, 'trial sequences require a supervised controller launch'
end
if controlled && (trial.nil? || dry || mode || !options.empty? || name.match?(/\Abounty\z/i))
  raise EO::Engine::Controller::Invalid, 'controlled eohunter requires one reviewed profile and one bounded trial sequence'
end
world = EO::Engine::World.new
# bandit mode from the word or from the bounty (bigshot 3357, 3824):
# Lich's Bounty::Task says whether the task is a bandit one
bounty_task = world.bounty_task
# ;eohunter bounty: ebounty's hunt child in place of "bigshot bounty"
# (bigshot 3355-3361): the profile ebounty loaded into UserVars.op, with
# its targets and rooms already rewritten for the task (ebounty
# go_hunting 2264-2279) and its bounty_eval (set_eval 2078); "bounty
# <creature>" is ebounty's ranger_track (2286).
bounty_mode = name =~ /\Abounty\z/i ? true : false
if bounty_mode
  op = UserVars.op.to_h
  if op.empty?
    EOHunter.msg('error', 'bounty mode: UserVars.op is empty; ebounty loads the profile before starting the hunt')
    exit
  end
  profile = EO::Engine::Profile.new(op, name: op['profile_current'].to_s, uid_ids: ->(uid) { world.uid_ids(uid) })
  options = ['track', options.first] if options.first && options.first !~ /^dry$/i
  bounty_eval = op['bounty_eval'].to_s
  # bigshot set_bounty_eval 3834-3836 when ebounty left none
  if bounty_eval.empty?
    bounty_eval = %q{!!(checkbounty =~ /^You.*?(succeeded|located|failed )|your task is failed/ && checkmind != 'saturated' && !$bigshot_bandits)} +
                  %q{ || !!(checkbounty =~ /^You.*?(succeeded|located|failed )|your task is failed/ && $bigshot_bandits)} +
                  %q{ || !!(checkbounty =~ /^You are not currently assigned / && !Effects::Cooldowns.to_h.include?('Next Bounty'))}
  end
  # set_bandit_hunting 6888. Assigned both ways: bigshot sets it false at
  # script init (607) and ebounty clears it only at its own exit, so a
  # bandit child followed by an ordinary one in the same Lich session
  # left the flag set - and the ordinary task then ran with the bandit
  # clause of bounty_eval (which rests at "succeeded" with no fried or
  # mind guard) and the bandit-present hold below.
  $bigshot_bandits = EO::Engine::Tracking.bandit_task?(bounty_task) ? true : false
else
  path = EOHunter.profile_path(name)
  unless File.exist?(path)
    EOHunter.msg('error', "no profile at #{path}")
    exit
  end
  profile = EO::Engine::Profile.load(path, uid_ids: ->(uid) { world.uid_ids(uid) })
end
tracking = EO::Engine::Tracking.policy_from(options.reject { |o| o =~ /^dry$/i }, task: bounty_task)
controlled&.admit_profile!(profile)
trial&.admit_profile!(profile)

if mode == 'tail'
  exit if dry
  member = EOHunter.follow(mode_args)
  behaviors = EOHunter.build_follower(profile, world, member)
  engine = EO::Engine::Engine.new(world: world, behaviors: behaviors.values_at(:survival, :cleanse, :flee, :rest, :loot, :loadout, :maintain, :engage, :wander))
  EOHunter.wire(engine, behaviors)
  checked_at = Time.now
  engine.on_tick do |w|
    member.report(EO::Engine::Group.report(w, name: Char.name, rest_policy: behaviors[:rest_policy], counters: behaviors[:counters],
                                              sneaky: behaviors[:sneaky], looting: behaviors[:loot].looting?,
                                              rest_prep_done: behaviors[:rest].rest_prep_done,
                                              forced: behaviors[:rest].forced_reason,
                                              bounty: bounty_mode ? EO::Engine::Group.bounty_state(w) : nil))
    if Time.now - checked_at > 5
      checked_at = Time.now
      engine.stop!(:leader_lost) unless member.leader_alive?
    end
    engine.stop!(:leader_lost) if member.lost?
  end
  # the report again between ticks, so a blocking action never reads as a lost follower
  member.keep_alive!
  # the watch, from the running script (Lich removes a dead script's hooks)
  EO::Engine::Watch.install!
  before_dying do
    engine.stop!(:script_killed)
    member.stop_pulse!
    # the follower's own service, started at the join above
    DRb.stop_service
    EO::Engine::Watch.uninstall!
    EO::Engine::Events.reset!
  end
  engine.run
  member.stop_pulse!
  exit
end

leader = mode == 'head' && !dry ? EOHunter.lead(profile, world, mode_args) : nil
owner = Script.current
if controlled
  token = "#{Process.pid}:#{owner.object_id}:#{Process.clock_gettime(Process::CLOCK_MONOTONIC)}"
  controller_snapshot = -> { EOHunter.controller_snapshot(owner, token) }
  controller_guard = EO::Engine::Controller::Guard.new(owner: owner, snapshot: controller_snapshot, launch: controlled)
  children = EO::Engine::Controller::ChildScripts.new(owner: owner, guard: controller_guard)
end
behaviors = EOHunter.build(profile, world, tracking: tracking, leader: leader, scripts: children, trial: trial)
EOHunter.report(profile, behaviors)
EOHunter.msg('info', "bandit mode: only #{EO::Engine::Tracking::BANDIT_NOUNS.source.tr('|', ' ')} on the quick routine, no fleeing") if tracking.bandits?
EOHunter.msg('info', "tracking #{tracking.creature_name} before each step") if tracking.tracking?
EOHunter.msg('info', "bounty mode on profile #{profile.name}: #{world.bounty_text}") if bounty_mode
exit if dry
if behaviors[:area].too_big?
  EOHunter.msg('error', 'refusing to hunt with an unbounded area; add a boundary')
  leader&.finish!(:unbounded_area)
  exit
end

engine = EO::Engine::Engine.new(world: world, behaviors: behaviors.values_at(:survival, :cleanse, :flee, :muster, :rest, :loot, :loadout, :maintain, :engage, :wander).compact)
EOHunter.wire(engine, behaviors)
rest = behaviors[:rest]
engage = behaviors[:engage]
if leader
  engine.on_tick { |w| leader.publish(w, phase: rest.resting? ? :resting : :hunting, target: engage.target) }
  # the heartbeat again between ticks, so a blocking action never reads as a dead leader
  leader.keep_alive!
end
if bounty_mode
  # bigshot's bounty mode: bounty_check? after every command set (7862) is
  # a forced rest; with a group the leader's verdict decides (a lost
  # member ends the hunt, complete only when every member is); at the
  # resting room, prepped, the child exits for ebounty (7578); a child
  # contact ends it at once (7458).
  bounty_done = lambda do |w|
    # bounty_check? 8901: not while a bandit is still here
    next false if $bigshot_bandits && w.room.targets.any? { |t| t.type.to_s =~ /bandit/ }

    @CORRECT_PERCENT_MIND = w.me.fxp_pct
    eval(bounty_eval, binding) ? true : false
  rescue StandardError => e
    EOHunter.msg('error', "bounty_eval raised #{e.class}: #{e.message}")
    false
  end
  checked_at = Time.now - 10
  engine.on_tick do |w|
    next if Time.now - checked_at < 2

    checked_at = Time.now
    own = bounty_done.call(w)
    if leader && !leader.solo?
      # the group's verdict alone decides: the leader's own completion
      # never rests the group while a follower is unfinished
      own = case leader.bounty_decision(own)
            when :member_lost then engine.stop!(:member_lost); false
            when :rest then true
            else false
            end
    end
    rest.rest!('Bounty should be complete/ready') if own && !rest.resting?
    if w.bounty_text =~ /^You have made contact with the child you are to rescue/ && w.room.creatures.any? { |n| n.name.to_s =~ /child/i }
      EOHunter.msg('warn', 'exiting: bounty mode with child rescue')
      engine.stop!(:child_rescue)
    end
  end
  EO::Engine::Events.on(:rested) { engine.stop!(:bounty_rest) }
end
# The watch subscribes to Lich's parser seam from the running script,
# since Lich removes a dead script's subscriptions and hooks.
EO::Engine::Watch.install!
before_dying do
  # Teardown only. Lich kills the script's worker threads - the DRb server
  # among them - before it runs these procs (script.rb 2173, then 2191),
  # so a bounded wait for follower acks here can never collect one: it
  # spent the full deadline and reported every follower unacked, on a
  # plain ;kill as much as on a real stop. The acknowledged shutdown runs
  # from the run path below, while the threads are still alive.
  engine.stop!(:script_killed)
  leader&.stop_pulse!
  # The fallible steps last, each isolated: Lich rescues per proc but not
  # Interrupt, so a raise or an interrupted sleep here used to skip the
  # watch teardown and leave tracker handlers building a World per combat
  # line until the next eohunter start evicted them by name.
  begin
    leader&.finish!(engine.stop_reason || :script_killed)
    # The listening socket outlives the script: DRb.start_service replaces
    # the primary without closing the old server, so a restart in the same
    # Lich leaves the previous run's Hub still answering hunt_id, register
    # and report from a dead roster. stop_service closes the current one.
    DRb.stop_service if leader
    fput('movement autosneak off') if profile['sneaky_sneaky'] # bigshot 3374
  ensure
    EO::Engine::Watch.uninstall!
    EO::Engine::Events.reset!
    # the lambda closes over this run's engine; a restart sets its own
    EO::Engine::Actions::Base.interrupt = nil
  end
end

if controlled
  EOHunter.run_controlled(engine: engine, behaviors: behaviors, world: world, owner: owner,
                          launch: controlled, children: children, guard: controller_guard,
                          objective: trial, snapshot: controller_snapshot)
else
  # bigshot pre_hunt: prep commands, scripts, rally rooms, the hunting room
  behaviors[:rest].start!
  engine.run
  # The acknowledged shutdown, here rather than in before_dying: the DRb
  # server thread is still alive on this path, so a follower can actually
  # answer the hunt_over. An external ;kill cannot be acknowledged - the
  # threads are gone before any at_exit proc runs - and before_dying's
  # finish! covers that case without blocking.
  leader&.end_hunt(engine.stop_reason || :hunt_over)
end
